@startuml
title Transfer between two holders — what is private and what is published

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ActorBorderColor #4A78B5
}

actor "Holder A\n(sender)" as A
box "Private — proved on A's own device, never seen by the network" #F4F8FC
participant "transfer_private_to_private\n(from, to, amount)" as Priv
end box
database "Public state\npause, roles, total_supply,\nfreeze and list flags" as PS
box "Public — run by the sequencer, in the clear" #FDF4F4
participant "_transfer()" as Pub
end box
actor "Holder B\n(recipient)" as B
participant "Issuer" as I

A -> Priv : transfer(to = B, amount)

group Compliance, checked in private
  Priv -> PS : read the freeze and list flags of A and of B
  note right of PS
    Read as a value guaranteed stable for a known window
    (DelayedPublicMutable), because a proof is built against
    a past state. A change takes effect after the delay.
  end note
  Priv -> Priv : refuse if either party is frozen\nor fails the enabled list
end

group Move the value, in private
  Priv -> Priv : spend A's notes, create A's change note\nand B's new note
  Priv -> A : change note
  Priv -> B : new note + Transfer event
  Priv -> I : copy of both notes, and the Transfer event
  note right of I
    The issuer's audit trail. The contract cannot read a
    holder's balance, so the issuer is sent its own copy.
  end note
end

Priv -> Pub : enqueue _transfer()  — no arguments
Pub -> PS : assert the contract is not paused

note over A, I
  **What an observer learns:** that a transfer of this token happened.
  **Not**: who sent it, who received it, or how much.
  The public half carries no arguments, and `total_supply` does not move.
  A pause makes the public half revert, which reverts the private half with it.
end note

@enduml
